WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:03.003
Ukrainian president Zelensky turned 45

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.670
on Wednesday

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.105
and got one of his biggest

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.439
birthday wishes

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.440
when President Biden

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.742
announced that the United States

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:09.809
would send 31

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.812
M1 Abrams tanks to help with the fight.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.881
Dozens more leopard tanks

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.883
will come from Germany and other allies.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.885
Ukraine had long been pleading

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:21.054
for such heavy weapons from the West.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.122
And this breakthrough came

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.391
after what seemed to be a game of chicken

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.226
between the United States and Germany

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.827
to see who would offer their tanks.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:28.795
First,

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:29.996
let's talk about the war

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.698
and much more with today's terrific

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.732
global panel.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.000
Anne-Marie Slaughter

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.568
is the former director of policy

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.237
planning at the State Department

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.571
and joins us from Princeton.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.640
She is the president of New America.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.075
Carl Bildt is a former prime

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.009
minister of Sweden

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.911
and joins us from Stockholm.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.478
And Kishore

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.613
Mahbubani is a former

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.715
top Singaporean diplomat

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.717
and joins us from Singapore.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.552
Anne-Marie, what do you make of this,

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.254
particularly the

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.056
German decision

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.992
Well, the German decision

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.026
is extraordinary

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.861
in just historical terms,

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.630
because, once again,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.432
German tanks, Panzers.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.633
Do most of the Russians

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.901
and the Europeans

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.403
will be fighting Russia.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.038
They will not be rolling into Russia,

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.641
or at least we certainly hope not.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.243
So the kind of historical significance

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.078
is enormous.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.446
Really, though,

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.847
what's most important about this

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.248
decision is political.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:25.385
It is signaling to Putin, no,

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.986
we are not going to split,

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.155
we're going to maintain cohesion

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.790
and we're going to amp up.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.192
So we're not scared

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.294
of your threats of escalation.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.596
That's a more important signal right now

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.364
than the actual military advantage.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.166
It's going to take months

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.101
for the Ukrainians

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.203
to get them and to be able to use them

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.771
longer term.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.606
It will help Ukraine defend

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.241
and actually advance against Russia,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.043
but that's going to take quite a while.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.077
So for now,

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:54.080
it's really a very important political

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.484
signal that NATO's holding together.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.220
But Karl, if it is an important

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.187
political signal,

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.021
does it break

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:02.922
the stalemate

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.125
that seems to have developed

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.292
on the ground?

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.160
There is no, no,

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.229
no major advances on either side.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.197
Will this change that

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:12.665
over time?

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.333
It might,

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.400
but as Anne-Marie said,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.602
that's going to take quite some time.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.870
I think the immediate

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.205
significance is primarily the political,

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.640
and I think it was very important

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.575
that there were you as thanks as well.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.144
I think that is

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.512
in terms of political signal,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.247
even more important than

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.314
the German tanks.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.883
That might be one leopards,

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.751
which militarily is significant.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.586
But the fact that there are some problems

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.954
is also significant.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.323
That is going to take some months at best

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.425
to make sort of effective

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.828
fighting units out of this.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.796
And that will make it more possible

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.098
for the Ukrainians first

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.534
to resist the new Russian offensive

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:48.301
that is going to come

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.669
at some point in time.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.006
And then perhaps to be able to we control

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.207
take back

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.308
some of the territory

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.610
that Russia is trying to steal from them.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.012
Kishore,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:02.015
do you think that this play pushes Russia

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.650
in a direction

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.653
where it is more likely to negotiate?

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.821
So far, President Putin has not seemed

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.557
particularly willing to negotiate

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.161
Well, clearly,

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:20.133
the war has to be condemned.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.369
Russia's invasion has to be condemned.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:26.739
But I think Russia is also aware

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.843
that 85% of the world's population

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:34.280
has not imposed sanctions on Russia.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.516
And if you look at it functionally,

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.117
in terms of Russia's

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.253
links with the rest of the world,

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.455
they haven't been that badly damaged

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.823
by the war.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.824
So I don't think the

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:47.961
supply of additional weapons is going

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.262
to change everything

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.231
at the end of the day.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.900
It has to be a political compromise.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.235
And I think the vast

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.803
majority of the world would like to see

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.705
some kind of political compromise

00:03:58.705 --> 00:03:59.539
to end the war,

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:00.139
because the war

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:02.875
is damaging all of us, too.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.110
What do you say to that, Anne-Marie?

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.178
Is there a compromise

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.347
to be had in other words,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.682
some kind of deal where,

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.085
let's say

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:15.121
Crimea is what is given to the Russians

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.490
and in return for that, Russia recognizes

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.524
most of Ukraine.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.559
I mean, we you know,

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.194
diplomats can work out the formula.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.095
But the question is,

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.397
is that kind of political deal?

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.866
The the the only way to end this war

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.337
I see no sign of that.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.071
I mean, yes,

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.539
we can all outline

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.508
different possible deals.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.643
But in fact,

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:40.647
the Ukrainian position has hardened

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.481
and expanded.

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:42.482
I mean, wanting now

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.450
really total victory, wanting

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.953
not just the Donbas back,

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.821
but also Crimea.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.724
And I see no face-saving way

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.193
for Putin to climb down.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.129
The certainly the stalemate

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.730
militarily means

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.400
both sides can stick to their demands.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.970
The more doing things like sending tanks

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.706
helps Putin with his domestic audience

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.941
because his view is this is a narrow

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.777
proxy war against Russia.

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.512
So the more narrow does,

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.579
the stronger he get.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:17.350
So I don't see the actual psychologic

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.085
political conditions

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:21.120
more or the military ones

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.654
that make

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.256
any kind of deal likely

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:25.425
for the foreseeable future.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.694
Carl, where does this go?

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.462
It does sound like

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.596
I think Russia is right

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.365
that the Russians Putin seems

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:34.901
to have settled down for a long war

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.903
and essentially destroying

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.905
Ukrainian civilian infrastructure,

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.406
hoping to effectively defeat

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:41.574
the Ukrainian nation

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.576
rather than the army.

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:44.711
Well, I think that's correct.

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:45.545
Putin has tied

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.146
his entire political future

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.314
to the success

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:49.849
of getting rid of Ukraine,

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:52.018
which is what he wants to sort of restore

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.853
a greater Russian empire

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:54.887
that was there in the past

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:55.922
that he sees

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.890
as his destiny talks about life

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.392
and the death struggle.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.894
And there is no sign of him backing down

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.596
and there is no sign of the Ukrainians

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:04.197
to surrender.

